{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/792210-are-real-police-psychics-a-breach-of-the-veil-masquerade-paradigm","id":792210,"title":"Are REAL police psychics a breach of the Veil, Masquerade, Paradigm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T09:07:14-08:00","id":792210,"title":"Are REAL police psychics a breach of the Veil, Masquerade, Paradigm?","content":"So, I have a couple ideas for using a police psychic NPC, possibly a Thrall who sold his soul for Lore of Awakening 1 and Patterns 2, but would a police psychic that was the real deal be allowed to survive in the WoD? This seems like a grey area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T09:35:10-08:00","id":792226,"title":"","content":"Not really, although they are not an accepted police practice some departments might have a few &quot;consultants&quot; on call for cases. Granted the detective that uses them might be viewed as a joke by his fellow officers but results are results...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T09:38:42-08:00","id":792227,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that police psychics are well tolerated, since the vast majority of people consider them quacks that use standard cold reading tricks to be right often enough to fool the gullible (aka just like the real world).<br /> <br /> For groups seeking to hide (or worse) knowledge of the supernatural, these sorts of things advance a narrative that non-scientific methods aren't really supernatural powers, but perfectly mundane frauds and luck. They're ready to be debunked to show the superiority of a non-supernatural view of the world.<br /> <br /> For groups that are seeking to use supernatural powers covertly (which may or may not overlap with the first group), they also create a cultural trope to play into to keep themselves hidden. Play up being a police psychic and people assume you're a quack/fraud, but you've conned your way into access to all sorts of sensitive information to make you fake predictions look true... when you're really using powers instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:20:06-08:00","id":792460,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda curious how you differentiate people with powers, quacks and people with amazing deductive skills? Especially considering the first category will be insanley rare to the point that most splats won't even know something like that exists. It really doesn't seem like it's an actual area of concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:33:06-08:00","id":792466,"title":"","content":"There are a lot more violent crimes committed in the world of darkness than ours because you have vampires, werewolves and other supernaturals running around. Even mundane crime can often be traced back to them, because any criminal organization of note has kindred pulling the strings. A psychic cop is going to start uncovering this quick, and as such is a definite threat to the masquerade. As soon as the powers that be become aware of him, they're gonna come gunning for him with all they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T02:34:11-08:00","id":792681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/792210-are-real-police-psychics-a-breach-of-the-veil-masquerade-paradigm#post792210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a couple ideas for using a police psychic NPC, possibly a Thrall who sold his soul for Lore of Awakening 1 and Patterns 2, but would a police psychic that was the real deal be allowed to survive in the WoD? This seems like a grey area.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Plenty of Numina Psychics do this without being murdered by Hit Marks, of course plenty of Malks and tremere have as their backstory &quot;was psychic and got noticed&quot; Honestly I'd say its more an issue of what they direct things toward vs how they do it. There's plenty of pure human evil in the WOD without hitting anyone who cares about cleaning up supernatural issues","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T06:19:19-08:00","id":794128,"title":"","content":"Psychics are sometimes considered by Garou to be a natural phenomenon and thus not inherently a veil breach, but they're also sometimes considered too dangerous to let live, regardless as to whether they're a veil breach or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T00:36:14-08:00","id":795453,"title":"","content":"In and of themselves, if they are not a creature upon whom the Masquerade/Veil/etc is told to, then they aren't really beheld to it the same way. A mortal with Numina might still get offed by a Supernatural because of the Masquerade/Veil/etc because their existence (and theoretical lack of adherence to any convention of secrecy, or one up to the standards of a given Supernatural individual) could indirectly cause issues. But, pedantically, it's the Supernatural maintaining their Masquerade/Veil/etc or otherwise making their un/lives easier, rather than the mortal breaching it. Secrecy is the binding force in crossover games, so unless the psychic was being discreet, they'd be pretty likely to end up as collateral, in my opinion. The World of Darkness isn't big on hope and chances, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T19:19:48-08:00","id":798059,"title":"","content":"In and of themselves, such psychics are not violating any of these secret conspiracies, although the Technocracy will probably try to eliminate their powers in the last stages of a successful Pogrom against the supernatural.<br /> <br /> If they uncover evidence of the supernatural and proceed to investigate individual vampires and such, then it's just like anyone else investigating such a person. The individual vampire or whomever being investigated may respond in some fashion, but I doubt anyone else will intervene.<br /> <br /> The fact is that within the setting, there are a large number of people who either possess supernatural powers of one kind, or have knowledge of the supernatural. The Masquerade and the Veil exist even though this is the case. Going after every one of these factions and eliminating them is usually more trouble than they are worth.<br /> <br /> The usual response when confronted with an organization or people who are aware is not to destroy them, but to leave them alone (see the Camarilla's attitude toward the Arcanum).<br /> <br /> The normal relations of the supernatural factions with each other seems to be, &quot;If you go after us, we will destroy you. But otherwise we will leave you alone.&quot;<br /> <br /> A psychic who investigates a vampire is a possible threat. But eliminating that threat might provoke an even worse investigation. You are really rolling a die. A better response is often (but not always) is avoidance combined with discrediting the threat if necessary. So the end result might be the death of the psychic. This is a real possibility. But it is not the only one. It really depends on the NPCs and PCs involved, and what makes most sense with the specific facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T17:56:50-08:00","id":799964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/792210-are-real-police-psychics-a-breach-of-the-veil-masquerade-paradigm?p=798059#post798059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In and of themselves, such psychics are not violating any of these secret conspiracies, although the Technocracy will probably try to eliminate their powers in the last stages of a successful Pogrom against the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, they might try to redirect them into &quot;special intelligence sections&quot; and such as part of an initiative to collect/subsume them for study and use in refining and working out the kinks of the technocratic paradigm, with maybe some &quot;mental expansion substances&quot;, &quot;subliminar engrams&quot; and a bunch of other concepts/technobabble to help in directing and controlling future access of the public to some of these capacities/resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T01:36:53-08:00","id":802931,"title":"","content":"Yep, while the hardcore philosophical materialists in ItX might balk at psionics, many parts of the Technocracy employ psychic powers themselves. An Extraordinary Citizen like a police psychic is recruitment material far more than they are a target for elimination, overall.<br /> <br /> ...Assuming they aren't sympathizing with, ah, shall we say, undesirable elements. Yes. The consequences would be most unfortunate. Necessary, but unfortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:15:56-08:00","id":803350,"title":"","content":"Even with ItX... psychics aren't off the table. I say this having played an ItX Psychic, who's powers were seen as an adaptation to the computer they installed in his head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:23:39-08:00","id":803411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/792210-are-real-police-psychics-a-breach-of-the-veil-masquerade-paradigm?p=803350#post803350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with ItX... psychics aren't off the table. I say this having played an ItX Psychic, who's powers were seen as an adaptation to the computer they installed in his head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would be pretty limiting on Iteration X's part - not to say tragically ironic - to wax so much poetic about the potential of expanding human capacity through transcedent hardware while utterly ignoring the mere possibility of evolution through expansion of the <i>inner software</i>, so to speak... machines with all the same parts can do quite different things depending on operating system and programs, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}